name macro_tree
describe Camera two metres from a trunk, looking at the canopy. The vegetation look shot, and the frame Prompt 007's sway and Prompt 005's foliage filtering will be judged against. Wind is left at its default because the point is what a moving canopy looks like.
backend both

# TAA off for every scenario that compares a capture against a golden. Measured, not assumed:
# with TAA on, vk-vs-vk moves 0.996% of pixels at this pose against a 1.5% gate, and with it off
# 0.341% -- see dev/harness/src/image_compare.hpp for the full four-case table.
option --no-taa

# Prompt 007 goal 344: --no-wind, and it is a CAPTURE-REPRODUCIBILITY requirement rather than a
# preference. Goals 333/335/338 put moving content in every frame -- a ground shimmer, swaying trees
# and grass -- driven by an animation clock that is the WALL CLOCK by default, so a golden of this
# pose stopped being reproducible. `--anim-step` makes the clock deterministic per FRAME and that is
# not enough on its own, because `capture end` lands on a different frame index between runs (goal
# 337 records that limit). Killing the wind for a golden-comparing capture is what the project
# already does for every wind A/B -- goal 332's own 0.0012% number was measured that way -- and it
# leaves the golden measuring everything else: terrain, tree shape, grass geometry, shading, LOD.
option --no-wind

pose_ground 64,16 -90 8 1.7
wait 2

capture end macro_tree

assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6
